---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import company from '../data/company.json';

const updated = 'July 13, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`Privacy Policy | ${company.name}`}
  description="How VersaCarte collects, uses and protects your personal information."
>
  <section class="section-studio pt-32 pb-24">
    <div class="container-main legal-prose">
      <p class="section-label" data-reveal>Legal</p>
      <h1 class="section-studio__title" data-reveal>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted" data-reveal>Last updated: {updated}</p>

      <div class="prose-studio mt-12" data-reveal>
        <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
        <p>
          VersaCarte ({company.domain}) is an app and web development studio. For privacy inquiries,
          contact us at <a href={`mailto:${company.email}`}>{company.email}</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>2. Information we collect</h2>
        <p>We may collect the following when you interact with our site or services:</p>
        <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
          <li>Name and email address when you submit a contact form, newsletter signup or resource download</li>
          <li>Project details you voluntarily provide in inquiries</li>
          <li>Technical data such as IP address, browser type and pages visited through analytics tools</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>3. How we use your information</h2>
        <p>We use your information to:</p>
        <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
          <li>Respond to inquiries and deliver requested services</li>
          <li>Send studio updates if you have opted in</li>
          <li>Improve our website and understand how visitors use it</li>
          <li>Comply with legal obligations</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>4. Legal basis</h2>
        <p>
          We process personal data based on your consent (for example, newsletter subscriptions),
          our legitimate interest in operating and improving our business and contractual necessity
          when you engage our services.
        </p>

        <h2>5. Sharing and processors</h2>
        <p>
          We do not sell your personal data. We may share information with trusted service providers
          such as email delivery, form handling, hosting and analytics platforms, only as needed to
          operate our site and services.
        </p>

        <h2>6. Data retention</h2>
        <p>
          We retain contact and project information for as long as needed to fulfill the purpose for
          which it was collected or as required by law. You may request deletion of your data at any
          time.
        </p>

        <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          Depending on your location, you may have the right to access, correct, delete or restrict
          processing of your personal data and to withdraw consent where applicable. Contact us to
          exercise these rights.
        </p>

        <h2>8. Cookies and analytics</h2>
        <p>
          We may use cookies and privacy-focused analytics to understand site usage. You can control
          cookies through your browser settings. Where required, we will request consent before
          enabling non-essential tracking.
        </p>

        <h2>9. International transfers</h2>
        <p>
          As a remote-first studio serving clients worldwide, your data may be processed in
          countries other than your own. We take reasonable steps to ensure appropriate safeguards
          are in place.
        </p>

        <h2>10. Changes</h2>
        <p>
          We may update this policy from time to time. The date at the top of this page indicates
          when it was last revised.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
